# What `docker build` never sees. Both Dockerfiles COPY named paths only, so
# this is not what keeps the image small — it is what keeps things out of the
# build CONTEXT, which the builder is handed whole before any COPY runs.
#
# The first block is the one that matters. On the server the image is built
# from the same folder that holds the live documents and the owner key
# (DEPLOY.md: deploy.sh keeps data/, backups/ and .env inside the clone), so
# without these lines every deploy would pack every script, every image and
# the key into the context — and one careless COPY away from an image layer.

# ---- live data and secrets: never in a context, never in an image ----
# deploy.sh refuses to build unless these three lines are here exactly as
# written, so reword the comments freely but not them.
data/
backups/
.env
.env.*
# A copy of the app with somebody's script saved into it, and scratch copies
# of the same (.gitignore says why each exists).
*.splitpage.html
_*.html

# ---- big, and nothing the build reads ----
.git/
**/node_modules
desktop/
dist/
.cache/
.claude/
.github/

# ---- written by the local launcher at runtime ----
.update/
update-status.json
